.KEY DIR/A,STEP/K
.BRA {
.KET }
; up-uhc install: the UHC tools for AmigaOS 3 (aget, UHCSearch and the get/search scripts), unmodified, in
; UP-Term:uhc, with the UHC: assign, its path and the UHCBIN environment variable
; Run by this archive's Install (an Installer script), which asks the questions:
;   Execute <archive>/Files/install.dos <archive>/Files [STEP <part>]
; From a Shell without Installer the same line installs everything. The Installer
; runs the parts one at a time with STEP (tests/test_dist_addons.py holds the two to
; the same list); the first part, check, stops the install when up-term.lha is
; missing or too old (the reason is in ENV:UPTCHECK).
FailAt 21
; the archive's Files drawer: every name below is relative to it
CD "{DIR}"
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Skip {STEP}
EndIf
; @include dist/common/@CHECKFRAG@
Lab copy-uhc
; The drawer userland/uhc (the author's archive uhctools_os3.lha, unmodified) goes to UP-Term:uhc.
; Copy of a drawer copies what is in it.
MakeDir >NIL: UP-Term:licenses
Copy userland UP-Term: ALL CLONE QUIET
If WARN
  Quit 20
EndIf
; UHC: and UHCBIN: assigned now and at every boot, as UHC's own UHC-Startup expects (it assigns UHC: from
; $UHCBIN and adds UHC:C and UHC:S to the path). A block in S:User-Startup that does it only while
; UP-Term:uhc is there, so one left behind by an Uninstall that could not take it out does no harm.
SetEnv UHCBIN UP-Term:uhc
Assign UHC: UP-Term:uhc
Path UHC:C UHC:S ADD
Search >NIL: S:User-Startup ";BEGIN uhc"
If WARN
  Echo >>S:User-Startup ";BEGIN uhc"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "If EXISTS UP-Term:uhc"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "  Assign UHC: UP-Term:uhc"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "  Path UHC:C UHC:S ADD"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "  SetEnv UHCBIN UP-Term:uhc"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "EndIf"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup ";END uhc"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
EndIf
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
; @include dist/common/record.dos
Echo "UHC installed: in an UP-Term window, for example  aget  (README.txt)."
